  "prefLabel": "Phy 304.01 Method of Applying for Initial Licensure",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Phy 304.01 Method of Applying for Initial Licensure. Applicants who wish, after passing the applicable national physical therapy examination, to apply for initial licensure as a physical therapist or a physical therapist assistant shall do so by completing and submitting:\n\n(a) The “Universal Application for Initial License” required by Plc 304.01, by providing the information specified by Plc 304.03;\n\n(b) The additional information and documentation specified by Plc 304.04;\n\n(c) The criminal history records check required by RSA 328-F:18-a; and\n\n(d) The initial license fee required by Plc 1002.39.\n\nSource. #9233, eff 8-22-08 ss by #10724, eff 11-22-14; ss by #10933, eff 9-18-15; ss by #12864, eff 9-10-19; ss by #14563, eff 6-20-26, EXPIRES: 6-20-36",
